      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, the seller has no say or obligation once the goods are safely on board the vessel, as risk of loss or damage has fully transferred to you (the buyer). If a delay occurs or an incident happens during the voyage, you are responsible for the costs and any claims related to that transit. You retain control over the freight insurer and must contact them directly to address issues arising after loading.",
