      "content": "Under CIF, while you bear the cost and risk once goods load, the seller must obtain \"institutional minimum\" marine insurance, so always verify the certificate is issued in the seller's name and covers at least 110% of the invoice value. Ensure the policy explicitly lists the specific cargo types as insured items rather than providing a vague \"ALL RISK\" or \"All Risks\" clause that might leave gaps. You must coordinate the insurance claims directly with the insurer, and if there are policy discrepancies, negotiate or terminate the contract before shipment begins.",
